course: dictionary
lesson: 7731
title: Context clues: pug
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pug is a small dog with a flat, wrinkly face, but you can work out a lot from the words around the word. «Tank and Biscuit, the pug from across the road, bark at each other on every walk» tells you that a pug is an animal that barks, so it must be a kind of dog.
explain: The second sentence adds more clues: «Pugs and bulldogs were bred for flatter and flatter faces, which squeeze their airways so they snore and can struggle to breathe.» Flat faces are a problem here, not just a look. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the hard word to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Pug also has an old meaning. Long ago it was short slang for a boxer, from the word pugilist. The context tells you which meaning is meant: a dog with a flat face and a curly tail is the everyday meaning, and a boxer would not bark on a walk.
fact: A pug is a small dog with a flat, wrinkly face, a curly tail and short fur.
fact: Pugs are usually pale brown with a black face, or all black.
fact: «A pug nose» means a short, turned-up nose.
fact: Pugs and bulldogs were bred for flatter faces, which can make breathing hard, so owners must keep pugs cool and not let them get too tired.
fact: Long ago, «pug» was old slang for a boxer, short for pugilist.
exercise: «Tank and Biscuit, the pug from across the road, bark on every walk.» What is a pug? | A large bird with long legs | A kind of road sign | *A small dog with a flat, wrinkly face | A small cake with icing
exercise: «Vets now advise choosing dogs with slightly longer noses.» Why? | Because longer noses are cheaper to feed | Because long noses smell better | *Because flat faces can squeeze the airways and make breathing hard | Because flat faces are too fashionable
exercise: Ella says a «pug nose» is a flat, squashed nose. What does the phrase really mean? | A short, turned-up nose | *A nose that is short and turned up | A long, thin, pointed nose | A nose that is always cold
test: What colour is a pug usually? | Blue with white spots | Bright green | *Pale brown with a black face
test: «Pug» was once short slang for which other thing? | *A boxer | A kitten | A petrol station
exam: Which clue in the text shows that pugs can have breathing problems? | The dog is pale brown | *«which squeeze their airways so they snore and can struggle to breathe» | Tank and Biscuit bark on every walk
